//< A generic function calling itself with a different type argument is stopped at a depth cap
//<
//< Without the cap the compilation does not finish. Call depth cannot measure it (each body goes
//< to the pending queue, so it returns to 0 per item), and each new mangled name misses the
//< instantiation cache (inst_chain_depth in ksplc/sema/session/ctx.kspls).
// EXPECT: generic function instantiation chain too deep
fn recur<|T|>(x: T)
  y: T[1]
  y[0] = x
  recur(y)

fn main()
  recur(1)
